Write a solution to swap the seat id of every two consecutive students. 
If the number of students is odd, the id of the last student is not swapped.
Return the result table ordered by id in ascending order.


SOLUTION:

SELECT LEAST(id + IF(id % 2 = 1, 1, -1), COUNT(*) OVER()) AS id, student
-- LEAST to get case of if it is the last entry in an odd amount of ids
-- IF case to decide whether a person should move up or down a seat depending on their modularity, resulting in swapping of seats in same sized groups as the mod function. 

FROM Seat
ORDER BY id ASC
